fmlib: complete the DEV_TO_ID handle-to-cookie conversions (ASK A103)

Post-A85 the kernel expects cookies at the ioctl boundary and cleanly
rejects raw userspace t_Device pointers (E_INVALID_SELECTION). fmlib
omitted the conversion at eight sites, leaving the affected verbs
unusable from userspace:

 - FM_PCD_CcRootBuild: FR next-engine arm (frm_replic_id)
 - FM_PCD_FrmReplicSetGroup / AddMember: nested-FR arm
 - FM_PCD_PlcrProfileSet: modify arm (profile_select.p_profile)
 - FM_PCD_ManipNodeReplace: p_next_manip (the NXP REMINDER comment)
 - FM_PORT_PcdKgModifyInitialScheme: scheme_id (direct arm)
 - FM_PORT_PcdPlcrModifyInitialProfile: profile cookie
 - FM_PORT_VSPAlloc: NULL p_fm_tx_port (ports are fd-based, not
   cookie-registered; the kernel derives the coupled Tx handle for Rx
   ports and refuses any userspace value)

Each conversion follows the file's established local idiom and the
kernel handler contract in lnxwrp_ioctls_fm.c. Whole-tree replacement
(PcdCcModifyTree) remains deliberately unsupported per A113.

